15 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Panel A illustrates the development of gd T cells in humans fromgestation to ten years, showing peaks of Vd2 in blood vessels and Vd1 in skin andintestinal epithelium. Panel B depicts the isolation of gd T cells from a healthy donor, theirin vitro expansion with IL-2 and zoledronic acid, and modeling under normal glucose or high glucose. Panel C shows gd T cell development in mice from gestationto two weeks postpartum, highlighting peaks of Vg5, Vg6, and other subtypes in varioustissues like epidermis, lung, and spleen.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (llustration showing the signaling pathways of gd T cells activated by Pathogen-sensing route and TCR-dependent route.  Antigens lead to activation of MAPK pathways. Dendritic cells and macrophagesrelease IL-23 and IL-1 cytokines, which engage with IL-1R/IL-23R, influencing pathwayswith JAK and leading to RoRgt activation. This results in IL-17 production.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Illustration depicting the interaction between Vy9V62 T cells and tumor cells. The diagram shows pathways involving glucose metabolism, lactate accumulation, and the role of AMPK in activating or inhibiting cellular processes. Metformin's influence on AMPK and ATP synthesis is indicated. The binding of phosphoantigens and components BTN3A1, BTN3A2, and BTN2A1 to tumor cells is illustrated, with arrows showing pathways and effects like tumor cell killing through perforin and granzymes. The mevalonate pathway and Warburg effect are also highlighted.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Diagram illustrating the pathophysiology of psoriasis in a patientwith Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus \(T2DM\). The skin layersinclude the epidermis and dermis. In the epidermis, keratinocytes are activated,increasing CCL20, which interacts with CCR6 on gd T cells. IL-23 and IL-17 are alsoelevated. GLP-1 can alleviate this pathological proces.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
